Image SXM history        v1.56 - v1.57        ( Feb 95 - Jul 95 )____________________________________________________________________________________v1.57    ∑9    ( 1 Jul 95 )   Added features:	•	A zoom feature has been added. By option-clicking in an image window, a small window is opened showing a magnified view of the region of the image around the cursor (default 2x magnification, 4x if the shift key is also pressed). If the click occurs close to a corner, the zoom window is placed in that corner, otherwise it is placed overlapping the right-hand edge of the image. The zoom window can be moved but not resized. The zoom image can be temporarily frozen by pressing the caps lock key. (Note that previously an option-click would select the largest square suitable for FFT operations. This selection is now made using control-click.)Bug fixes:	•	When an SEM image was loaded and auto resized, clicking in the window's zoom box would send the window offscreen. This bug has been fixed.Other changes:	•	The brightness and contrast of an image can now be changed by selecting the LUT tool and then pressing the caps lock key. Horizontal movement of the mouse changes the brightness and vertical movement changes the contrast. This method has an advantage over the conventional method (using the Map window) in that both the brightness and contrast can be changed continuously without any mouse clicks - some may find this convenient.____________________________________________________________________________________v1.57    ∑8    ( 20 Jun 95 )    Added features:	•	The 3d Plot dialog box now has the option of displaying a small preview of the plot. This makes setting the optimum values for the viewing angles easier. If the plot takes a long time to redraw every time the viewing angles are changed, try selecting the menu item with the Option key pressed – this will produce a smaller preview image which should be redrawn more quickly.Bug fixes:	•	None.Other changes:	•	All Image SXM dialog boxes now respond to the escape key (Cancel) in addition to the return key (OK).____________________________________________________________________________________v1.57    ∑7    ( 1 Jun 95 )   Added features:	•	None.Bug fixes:	•	Fixed a bug that caused the 3d Plot routine to execute even if the dialog box Cancel button was pressed.	•	Discovered an obscure bug that manifests itself when running under System 7.5 on Power Macs (and System 7.5.1 on a Performa 5200/6200). The symptom is that when there are no image or text windows open, the user cannot return to the Finder by clicking on the desktop. It seems to occur when the small memory display window is selected, and so can be cured simply by deselecting that window by clicking on the Info window. Circumvented the problem by selecting the Info window when Image SXM initialises and whenever the last window is closed. Note that running System 7.5.1 on a Power Mac doesn't produce this problem (the upgrade 7.5 -> 7.5.1 is free from Apple).Other changes:	•	The LUT saved in the 'Image SXM Prefs' file was not used as the default if it was one of the new palettes added in ∑1. Now any of the palettes available from the 'Color Table' menu item can be used as the default by selecting the desired palette and then either selecting 'Record Preferences' or saving the preferences using the 'SXM Preferences...' dialog box (see ∑6).	•	The position of the small memory display window (which defaults to the bottom right of the screen) is now saved in the 'Image SXM Prefs' file if 'Save Window Positions' is checked. The window can be moved by holding down the option key and dragging the window.____________________________________________________________________________________v1.57    ∑6    ( 8 May 95 )   Added features:	•	A new 'SXM Preferences...' item has been added to the Options menu. This dialog box allows quick access to all of the other options/preferences dialog boxes that are usually accessed from other menus. It also allows the user to reload the Preferences file to reset all the parameters without restarting Image SXM.Bug fixes:	•	In NIH Image v1.57 the profile plot scale of spatially uncalibrated images was set to zero. This caused problems with the latest version of the profile plot procedure as it uses this variable to plot the tick marks on the horizontal axis. Uncalibrated images now have the profile plot scale set to unity.  • The 3d Plot procedure calculated the wrong dimensions for the plot window if the azimuthal view angle was negative (i.e., viewed from the left). The bug has been fixed by taking the absolute value of the view angle.Other changes:	•	The preferences set in the SEM, STM, STS, SAM and 3d Plot dialog boxes are now saved in the preferences file when the 'Record Preferences' item is selected from the File menu. ____________________________________________________________________________________v1.57    ∑5    ( 1 May 95 )   Added features:	•	Balloon Help has been added to the SEM, STM and FFT menu items to aid new users of Image SXM.Bug fixes:	•	The routine that calculates the z scaling for STM images had an unnecessary rounding error. STM images are now scaled correctly, but PICT or TIFF files saved using earlier versions of Image SXM will have this z scaling error. It will only be apparent for very flat images that have a small variation in z over the entire image. Reloading the original STM images and resaving them will correct the scaling. As accurate measurements can only be made on images that have been recalibrated (using 'ReCalibrate Z', which was not affected by this bug), this should not have caused any problems.	•	Burleigh STM images with an x or y range > 32767 Å would display negative dimensions. Changing a signed integer to an unsigned integer fixed this bug. Other changes:	•	The routines that read the parameters from VG SAM image file headers have been changed so that they should work for all VG SAM files, not just the limited selection used to test version ∑3.	•	Zero-valued pixels are now ignored when calculating the minimum intensity of pixels in VG SAM images. Such pixels, which seem to occur occasionally due to glitches, caused problems in earlier versions. 	•	The STM Options dialog box now has an option for the dimensional units used in all displays - nm or Å. There is also a new checkbox for using µm for images larger than 1 µm in size.	•	Ticks have been added to both axes of profile plots to help with rough estimates of the size of features (accurate measurements are still displayed in the Info window as before).____________________________________________________________________________________v1.57    ∑4    ( 6 Apr 95 )   Added features:	•	None.Bug fixes:	•	In the non-FPU version of Image SXM the routine that reads floating point numbers from parameter files or image file headers sometimes gave the wrong results. The problem didn't arise in the FPU or PowerMac versions. It was traced to an incorrect evaluation of a transcendental function - a bug in CodeWarrior or SANE? The problem was circumvented by rewriting the routine.Other changes:	•	The spatial calibration of the 3d Plot window is now calculated from the calibration of the original image, so that a calibration bar can be added to the 3d Plot window if desired (see file 'Demo of 3d Plot'). As the effect of perspective in the 3d plot makes 'distant' features smaller than 'closer' features, don't rely on the spatial calibration for accurate measurements.____________________________________________________________________________________v1.57    ∑3    ( 31 Mar 95 )   Added features:	•	Image SXM can now read image files produced by the VG Scanning Auger Microscope (SAM) system. The image magnification, beam voltage and beam current settings are read from the parameter block at the start of the file (the first 369 bytes!). The peak (PEAK.DTI) and background (BGND.DTI) images can be loaded and displayed individually, or both can be loaded and the resultant Auger image (= (peak-bgnd)/bgnd) calculated automatically. The options are set in the 'SAM Options' dialog box accessed from the SEM menu. The images can be browsed using the 'Browse Images...' command in the SEM menu. As SAM images are usually much smaller than SEM images, the reduction factor should be kept small.Bug fixes:	•	None.Other changes:	•	The Image SXM variant can now be changed without modifying the code of Image SXM itself. If the filename of the application is changed to 'Image SXM', 'Image SEM', 'Image STM' or 'Image SAM' then the splash box will display the corresponding name and various menu shortcuts will be set as appropriate. 	•	Image SXM was given a Spring clean, removing redundant code and generally tidying things up a bit. The probability of introducing a bug in the process is not insignificant.____________________________________________________________________________________v1.57    ∑2    ( 24 Mar 95 )    Bug fixAdded features:	•	None.Bug fixes:	•	Fixed a bug that caused the dialog box for 'Change File Types...' to hang.Other changes:	•	None. ____________________________________________________________________________________v1.57    ∑1    ( 20 Mar 95 )    General releaseAdded features:	•	A number of extra palettes have been added to the 'Color Tables' submenu in the Options menu. These were available previously as separate files that could be loaded in when needed. They have been placed in this menu for convenience.Bug fixes:	•	ReCompensation for x and y tilt now works correctly on Burleigh STM images.	•	Changing the contrast/brightness settings on a Burleigh STM image no longer removes the z calibration.Other changes:	•	The 'Shadow Plot...' menu item in the STM menu has been replaced with '3d Plot...'. The routine has been rewritten from scratch for maximum computational speed - an improvement of about x6 has been achieved, so that plots of a 256x256 image can be produced in 15 s on a Quadra, or 3 s on a PowerMac. The new routine produces a 3d plot of the surface, allowing the user to specify the direction from which the surface is viewed. The colours used for each pixel in the 3d plot can be taken from the original image LUT or from a calculation of the illumination of the surface from a light source in a specified direction. A third option calculates the effect of the specified illumination but doesn't produce the 3d plot. Once the 3d plot has been drawn, the view angles can be altered in increments of 10° using the four cursor keys. Holding down the Option key moves the viewpoint by 30°. Holding down the Shift key when pressing the up/down cursor keys increases/decreases the z magnification factor.	•	FFTs can now be calculated for images up to 512x512 providing that 6 Mbytes of free memory are available. The default maximum FFT size is 256x256, but this can be changed from the FFT menu if required. ____________________________________________________________________________________v1.57    ß2    ( 12 Feb 95 )    Development versionAdded features:	•	A new 'Add Axes and LUT' procedure has been added to the 'Images' submenu of the STM menu. This adds a border to the image window, adds x and y axes, and displays the look-up table (LUT) of the image. The font, size and style of the text used can be set in the 'Options' menu. Bug fixes:	•	NIH Image v1.57 fixes a number of bugs present in v1.55. See the NIH Image documentation for details.Other changes:	•	As Image SXM now has the ability to read STM files of different formats (i.e., Omicron or Burleigh), the manufacturer's name is now stored in the image header. Images saved by previous versions of Image SXM will be read as 'NotSpec', meaning that the manufacturer is not specified. This should not have any serious effect on subsequent analysis of the image.	•	Separate calibration files are now used for Omicron and Burleigh STM images. The original calibration file is still supported for handling images saved with previous versions of Image SXM. All the data from the calibration files are loaded when Image SXM starts up. When recalibrating or applying a previous calibration, the data appropriate to the image being analysed are used.	•	In combining the source code for NIH Image v1.57 with that written for Image SXM, a large number of changes have been made. Apart from the added features noted above, most of these changes are cosmetic and should not result in any differences in the execution of the application compared to Image SXM v1.55. However, in 56 000 lines of code some errors are inevitable. This version is labelled a 'beta' version until it has been checked more thoroughly on other Macs.____________________________________________________________________________________